'' A TIKO DLL'S STRING RESULTS STAY RIGHT PAST 256 CALLS (review RT-01). The host frees each
'' result's data and releases the descriptor to its own runtime, so the DLL's pool never got
'' it back: from the 257th call every result was "" (total 2196 = 1+...+256 with fbc too).
'' tiko-rt grows a spent pool instead -- a deliberate divergence from fbc -- and says so once.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' CLEAN: build/.dls
'' COPY: tests/driver/src/dllstr => build/.dls/src
'' STEP: -target windows-x86_64 -dll build/.dls/src/words.bas -o build/.dls/src/words.dll
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 build/.dls/src/app.bas -o build/.dls/src/app.exe
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: build/.dls/src/app.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: tiko-rt: the string temporary pool was exhausted and has grown
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: total 1203
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: empty 0
